          "page": 5,
          "section": "3.1.2. EDS analysis of the NbTaV samples",
          "quote": "Rather, the inconsistency between the nominal and measured chemical composition of the NbTaV alloy was attributable to the significant difference in the densities of the constituent elements: Nb (8.57 g/cm3), Ta (16.68 g/cm3), and V (6.11 g/cm3). While the initial powder mixture had a composition close to the equiatomic one, its handling to the hopper could result in demixing. Thus, the denser Ta powder was likely settled to the bottom of the hopper and was consequently consumed first during the deposition process.",
